---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Inventory & Warehousing — Stock Tracking, Valuation, Multi-Location"
  description="Item catalogue, stock tracking, FIFO and weighted-average costing, GRN, transfers, reorder levels, and multi-location warehousing. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/inventory/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm"><div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Inventory & Warehousing</li></ol></nav>
    <h1>Inventory & Warehousing</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-subtext">Know what you have, where it is, what it cost, and when to reorder. One stock ledger, updated in real time across every location.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Warehouse managers, store supervisors, procurement officers, and operations leaders who need accurate stock visibility across locations — without reconciling spreadsheets at month end.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Item Catalogue</h3><p>Maintain a structured catalogue with categories, unit of measure, reorder levels, preferred suppliers, and GL account mappings. Support raw materials, finished goods, packaging, and consumables.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Stock Valuation</h3><p>Value stock using FIFO or weighted average cost. Automatically recalculate on receipt. Generate valuation reports by item, category, or location. Post valuation adjustments to the GL.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Goods Received Notes</h3><p>Record goods received against purchase orders. Match quantities and prices. Flag discrepancies for review. GRN triggers automatic stock increase and GL posting.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Multi-Location Warehousing</h3><p>Manage stock across warehouses, shops, factory floors, and transit locations. View stock by location or consolidated. Transfer stock between locations with approval workflows.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Batch & Expiry Tracking</h3><p>Track items by batch number and expiry date. Apply FEFO (first-expiry-first-out) picking rules. Generate expiry alerts. Essential for food, pharmaceutical, and perishable goods.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>UOM Conversion</h3><p>Purchase in cases, sell in pieces, store in kilograms. The conversion engine automatically translates between units. All ledger entries are recorded in the base UOM for consistency.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Reorder Alerts</h3><p>Set minimum and reorder levels per item per location. Generate purchase requests automatically when stock falls below threshold. Never run out of critical items.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Stock Reports</h3><p>Stock summary, stock aging, movement history, valuation reports, and reorder level reports. All reports exportable to PDF and Excel. Drill down from summary to transaction detail.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>Sales</strong> → stock is deducted automatically on delivery confirmation</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement</strong> → stock increases on goods receipt, matched to purchase orders</li>
      <li><strong>Manufacturing</strong> → raw materials consumed, finished goods received on production completion</li>
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → every stock movement posts to the general ledger automatically</li>
      <li><strong>Sales Agents</strong> → separate agent stock tracking with consignment and commission management</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Controls and permissions</h2>
    <div class="controls-grid">
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Store-Level Access</h3><p>Restrict users to specific stores or locations. A warehouse supervisor in Kampala cannot access Mombasa stock without explicit permission.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Approval Workflows</h3><p>Stock adjustments, transfers, and write-offs require approval. Configure thresholds and approval chains per location.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Immutable Ledger</h3><p>Every stock transaction is recorded in the stock ledger. No deletion, only reversal. Full traceability from receipt to dispatch.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>GL Integration</h3><p>Every inventory movement posts to the general ledger. Stock valuation, adjustments, and transfers are always reflected in the financial records.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Store Dashboard</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Stock Summary</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Stock Valuation</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Batch Expiry Tracking</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See inventory in action</h2><p>Request a demonstration tailored to your warehousing and stock management needs.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero{padding:var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12)}.page-hero h1{font-size:var(--kc-text-4xl);max-width:700px}.page-hero-subtext{font-size:var(--kc-text-lg);color:var(--kc-text-secondary);max-width:60ch;margin-top:var(--kc-space-4)}.breadcrumb ol{list-style:none;padding:0;display:flex;gap:var(--kc-space-2);font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-6)}.breadcrumb a{color:var(--kc-teal);text-decoration:none}.breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after{content:'/';margin-left:var(--kc-space-2);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary)}.container--narrow{max-width:var(--kc-container-narrow)}.container--narrow p{font-size:var(--kc-text-base);color:var(--kc-text-secondary);line-height:var(--kc-leading-relaxed);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-4)}.feature-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:var(--kc-space-6);margin-top:var(--kc-space-8)}.feature-card{padding:var(--kc-space-6);background:var(--kc-surface-light);border:1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg)}.feature-card h3{font-size:var(--kc-text-lg);font-family:var(--kc-font-body);font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-2)}.feature-card p{font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-secondary)}.connection-list{margin-top:var(--kc-space-4)}.connection-list li{margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-3);font-size:var(--kc-text-base);color:var(--kc-text-secondary)}.connection-list strong{color:var(--kc-text-primary)}.controls-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:var(--kc-space-6);margin-top:var(--kc-space-6)}.control-item{padding:var(--kc-space-5);border-left:3px solid var(--kc-teal)}.control-item h3{font-size:var(--kc-text-base);font-family:var(--kc-font-body);font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-1)}.control-item p{font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-secondary)}.screenshot-intro{color:var(--kc-text-secondary);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-6)}.screenshot-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:var(--kc-space-6)}.screenshot-placeholder{aspect-ratio:16/10;background:var(--kc-surface-warm);border:2px dashed var(--kc-border);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:var(--kc-space-2)}.screenshot-label{font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);color:var(--kc-text-primary)}.screenshot-note{font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary)}.btn--inverse{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);font-size:var(--kc-text-base);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg);background:transparent;color:var(--kc-text-inverse);border:2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);transition:all var(--kc-transition-fast);text-decoration:none;margin-top:var(--kc-space-6)}.btn--inverse:hover{background:var(--kc-teal);border-color:var(--kc-teal)}@media(max-width:768px){.page-hero h1{font-size:var(--kc-text-3xl)}.feature-grid,.controls-grid,.screenshot-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
